{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md | sed -n '666,677p;1002,1030p;1090,1110p'\nrg -n 'R5|B6|debruijn_register_linker|if R5|or B6|R5 together' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md\"","aggregated_output":"   666\tregisters, and a dead register is by definition never read again, so a\n   667\tlift-out has every value any pending frame can observe. What does not\n   668\tsurvive a round trip is pc identity, temporary ids, and dead values, all\n   669\tof which the stack design's section 1 already declines to promise.\n   670\tSecond, until that format exists, cross-host transport of a parked\n   671\tcontinuation is same-model only: a register continuation travels to a\n   672\thost with a register kernel, a stack continuation to a host with the\n   673\tstack VM, and each such transfer also needs the image by R or H through\n   674\tthe B6 linker. This rule is deliberate; the alternative was a pair\n   675\tof lossy lifts between two positional formats that the third VM would\n   676\thave made obsolete.\n   677\t\n  1002\tdeterministic stream/effect behavior. The pure-program tier may merge\n  1003\tbefore R2 lands; R4 is complete only when both tiers are.\n  1004\t\n  1005\tThe phase order runs on two parallel tracks after R1: on the register\n  1006\ttrack, R2's descriptor and liveness extension and R4's pure-program tier,\n  1007\tthen R4's effects tier once B4 and R2 exist, then R3 against the real\n  1008\tkernel; on the linker track, Phase B6 provides both stack and register\n  1009\tlinking over dao.stream, depending on R1 and B1/B2 only and free to land\n  1010\tbefore R2 or R4.\n  1011\t\n  1012\t### R5: linker integration over dao.stream\n  1013\t\n  1014\t    Fulfilled by: Phase B6 (src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc,\n  1015\t    test/yin/vm/debruijn_linker_test.cljc)\n  1016\t    Specification: docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md\n  1017\t    Must not change: stack H, dao.stream, dao.jing, dao.jing.dht\n  1018\t\n  1019\tPer the owner's directive (\"B6 should be used by both the stack and register\n  1020\tvm for linking code over dao.stream\"), the register format linking capabilities\n  1021\tare fulfilled directly within the unified B6 linker phase. Phase B6 delivers\n  1022\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc`, providing the parameterized `fetch`\n  1023\tfunction, the register format record (`:yin.debruijn.register`), the R index,\n  1024\tand same-root pairing datoms (`[root :yin.debruijn.register/hash R]`) with\n  1025\tboth trusted and verifying fallback paths. Full specification, file box,\n  1026\tand completion criteria are defined in `docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md`.\n  1027\t\n  1028\t## 7. Non-goals and protected surfaces\n  1029\t\n  1030\tThis design does not alter any B0-B7 phase's semantics, the stack VM, named\n  1090\t    shapes, and validation as pure data before R4 interprets them. The\n  1091\t    shared engine remains the sole owner of scheduling and wake disposition.\n  1092\t\n  1093\tDEFERRED:\n  1094\t\n  1095\t- Spill representation and register-file limits, if a target requires them.\n  1096\t- Register continuation lifting and cross-model park/resume transport.\n  1097\t- The B7 name-environment ledger and provenance that the B6 same-root\n  1098\t  pairing's trust rests on; R4 and B6 are both decided phases.\n  1099\t\n  1100\t## 9. End condition\n  1101\t\n  1102\tThe lowerer-only end condition is a validated, deterministic register image\n  1103\twhose R is reproducible on all three hosts, whose address law with the stack\n  1104\timage holds over the parity corpus, and whose named-VM normalized fixtures\n  1105\tagree. The full register-VM end condition adds a validator-approved kernel\n  1106\twith both R4 tiers complete, the R3 report published for the owner to read,\n  1107\tand cross-stream R fetch and verification via the B6 linker. The\n  1108\tproject does not stop at R2: R3's numbers inform, they do not decide.\n298:that B6's rule \"a fetched image may be executed by the semantic VM after\n674:the B6 linker. This rule is deliberate; the alternative was a pair\n1008:kernel; on the linker track, Phase B6 provides both stack and register\n1012:### R5: linker integration over dao.stream\n1014:    Fulfilled by: Phase B6 (src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc,\n1019:Per the owner's directive (\"B6 should be used by both the stack and register\n1021:are fulfilled directly within the unified B6 linker phase. Phase B6 delivers\n1097:- The B7 name-environment ledger and provenance that the B6 same-root\n1098:  pairing's trust rests on; R4 and B6 are both decided phases.\n1107:and cross-stream R fetch and verification via the B6 linker. The\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md | sed -n '1,40p;139,170p;202,242p;319,388p'\nrg -n 'debruijn_register_linker|R5|Phase B6|stack-free-names|register-free-names|segment-matches|make-get|client RPC|local storage' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md | sed -n '1,40p;139,170p;202,242p;319,388p'\nrg -n 'debruijn_register_linker|R5|Phase B6|stack-free-names|register-free-names|segment-matches|make-get|client RPC|local storage' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# yin.vm de Bruijn linker over dao.stream (Phase B6)\n     2\t\n     3\tStatus: design, revised; not implemented\n     4\t\n     5\t## 1. Objective and architectural position\n     6\t\n     7\tThis document specifies the closed-image code linker for `yin.vm` over\n     8\t`dao.stream` (backed by `dao.jing` content addressing). It is Phase B6 of\n     9\tthe de Bruijn compilation and VM architecture.\n    10\t\n    11\tGoverning rule: **B6 is used by both the stack VM and the register VM for\n    12\tlinking code over `dao.stream`.**\n    13\t\n    14\tFoundational principle: **The linker fetches code over `dao.stream`, but the\n    15\tcode itself is stored in `dao.jing`.**\n    16\t\n    17\tIn datom.world, code and continuations flow through streams: one universal\n    18\tAST, multiple execution backends (stack VM and register VM), peer witnesses\n    19\tto the same truth. Executable code is content-addressed data stored in\n    20\t`dao.jing`, while linking, resolution, and fetching occur strictly over\n    21\tappend-only `dao.stream` boundaries. Upstream stages -- Yang, the resolver\n    22\t(B2), the stack lowerer (B2), and the register compiler (R1, R2) -- produce\n    23\tcontent-addressed executable images:\n    24\t- Stack images, identified by H (`:yin.debruijn.code`)\n    25\t- Register images, identified by R (`:yin.debruijn.register`)\n    26\t\n    27\tThe linker is the component that enables either VM to resolve, fetch,\n    28\tverify, and link those executable images over `dao.stream`. A host holding\n    29\tonly an identity (H or R) and an index can obtain the image over a stream,\n    30\tprove it matches the storage address, prove it matches the requested\n    31\tcontract identity, validate its structural and liveness invariants, verify\n    32\tfree-variable closure for the receiving environment, and deliver it for\n    33\texecution.\n    34\t\n    35\tPhase B6 is implemented alone as the dedicated linker phase. It establishes\n    36\tthe format-parameterized fetch function (`yin.vm.debruijn-linker/fetch`) and\n    37\tprovides the concrete format records for both the stack and register VMs.\n    38\t\n    39\t## 2. Invariants: storage in dao.jing, fetching over dao.stream\n    40\t\n   139\t### 4.2 The six steps\n   140\t\n   141\tFetch executes six steps in strict order:\n   142\t\n   143\t```clojure\n   144\t;; (fetch handle index format identity)\n   145\t;; 1. address  <- (index identity)\n   146\t;;               absent entry            -> :absent\n   147\t;; 2. value    <- (jing/get handle address absent)\n   148\t;;               absent value            -> :absent\n   149\t;;               (not (jing/segment-matches? address value))\n   150\t;;                                       -> :address-mismatch\n   151\t;; 3.           (not= identity ((:hash-fn format) value))\n   152\t;;                                       -> :hash-mismatch\n   153\t;; 4.           ((:validate-fn format) value) returns a defect\n   154\t;;                                       -> that qualified defect\n   155\t;; 5.           ((:free-names-fn format) value) against receiver environment\n   156\t;;               unresolved name         -> :unresolved-free\n   157\t;;               name shadowed by store  -> :shadowed-free\n   158\t;; 6. return the verified image\n   159\t```\n   160\t\n   161\tStep order is load-bearing:\n   162\t\n   163\t1. Address verification (step 2) precedes identity verification (step 3)\n   164\t   because the storage address was requested from the store. Crucially,\n   165\t   `(jing/segment-matches? address value)` verifies the value against the\n   166\t   specific hash algorithm carried by `address`, rather than assuming\n   167\t   DaoJing's current minting default.\n   168\t2. Validation (step 4) precedes the closure check (step 5) so that\n   169\t   `:free-names-fn` only ever encounters structurally valid images. For\n   170\t   register images, step 4 includes the verified in-band live-set rules.\n   202\t## 5. Format records: stack and register\n   203\t\n   204\tB6 provides the format records for both execution backends:\n   205\t\n   206\t### 5.1 Stack format record (`:yin.debruijn.code`)\n   207\t\n   208\t```clojure\n   209\t{:format        :yin.debruijn.code\n   210\t :hash-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash\n   211\t :validate-fn   yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   212\t :free-names-fn yin.vm.debruijn-linker/stack-free-names}\n   213\t```\n   214\t\n   215\tThe payload stored in Jing is the canonical instruction vector value itself,\n   216\tat its own `segment-key`.\n   217\t- `image-hash` is B1's hash over the descriptor hash and canonical vector.\n   218\t- `image-defect` validates opcodes, operands, bounds, body arity chains,\n   219\t  and host scalar support.\n   220\t- `stack-free-names` is defined by the linker module (scanning `:load-free`\n   221\t  operands in the canonical vector), preserving \"Existing edits: none\".\n   222\t- The lift to `:yin.code/*` is `yin.vm.debruijn-linearize/lift`.\n   223\t\n   224\t### 5.2 Register format record (`:yin.debruijn.register`)\n   225\t\n   226\t```clojure\n   227\t{:format        :yin.debruijn.register\n   228\t :hash-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash\n   229\t :validate-fn   yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect\n   230\t :free-names-fn yin.vm.debruijn-linker/register-free-names}\n   231\t```\n   232\t\n   233\tThe payload stored in Jing is the register image map `{:bodies ...\n   234\t:instructions ...}`, at its own `segment-key`.\n   235\t- `register-hash` is R1's hash over the descriptor hash and register vector.\n   236\t- `register-image-defect` validates opcodes, register bounds, body ranges,\n   237\t  and the section 4.5 ascending, bounded, exact live sets.\n   238\t- `register-free-names` is defined by the linker module (scanning\n   239\t  `:load-free` operands across all bodies in the instruction vector),\n   240\t  preserving \"Existing edits: none\".\n   241\t- The lift to `:yin.code/*` is `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile/lift`.\n   242\t\n   319\t## 10. File box: Phase B6\n   320\t\n   321\t    New: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc\n   322\t    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn_linker_test.cljc\n   323\t    Existing edits: none\n   324\t    Depends on: dao.jing (segment-matches?, segment-key, materialize!, get),\n   325\t                dao.jing.dht (create-content-dht, IDhtNet),\n   326\t                dao.jing.remote (content-client, default-handlers),\n   327\t                B1 (image-hash, image-defect, descriptor),\n   328\t                B2 (lift),\n   329\t                R1 (register-hash, register-image-defect, descriptor, lift)\n   330\t    Must not change: merged projection namespace, image-hash, register-hash,\n   331\t                     dao.stream, dao.jing, dao.jing.dht, dao.jing.remote,\n   332\t                     named VM semantics\n   333\t\n   334\t`yin.vm.debruijn-linker` exports:\n   335\t- `fetch`: the parameterized fetch function.\n   336\t- `stack-format`: the `:yin.debruijn.code` format record.\n   337\t- `register-format`: the `:yin.debruijn.register` format record.\n   338\t- `stack-free-names`: scans free names from stack instruction vectors.\n   339\t- `register-free-names`: scans free names from register image maps.\n   340\t- `verify-same-root-pairing`: verifies an H and R pair against source datoms.\n   341\t- Qualified refusal constructors and predicates.\n   342\t\n   343\t## 11. Completion criteria: Phase B6\n   344\t\n   345\tCross-host transfer over `dao.stream`:\n   346\t\n   347\t1. (H, R) JVM to Dart transfer over `dao.jing.remote`'s DaoStream transport,\n   348\t   where the receiver initially knows only the identity (H or R) and an\n   349\t   index. Includes the Dart-side client harness for that path.\n   350\t2. (H, R) Equal normalized results under the B0 normalizer when the fetched\n   351\t   image is lifted and executed through the existing semantic VM, compared\n   352\t   to local execution.\n   353\t3. (H, R) The cross-host corpus is restricted to print-stable scalars until\n   354\t   CBOR lands; no golden test pins a Jing address.\n   355\t\n   356\tRefusals:\n   357\t\n   358\t4. (H, R) `:absent` for an identity the index cannot resolve.\n   359\t5. (H, R) `:address-mismatch` when the received value does not match the\n   360\t   address algorithm and digest, tested via:\n   361\t   a. Local storage corruption.\n   362\t   b. Corrupt client RPC response over DaoStream.\n   363\t6. (shared) A DHT peer serving mismatched content is rejected before load;\n   364\t   `make-get` filters invalid peer payloads, returning `:absent` if no peer\n   365\t   has valid data.\n   366\t7. (H, R) `:hash-mismatch` when a well-stored value at the indexed address\n   367\t   does not hash to the requested identity, including descriptor or contract\n   368\t   version disagreement.\n   369\t8. (H, R) Structural validator defect in a fetched image refused before load.\n   370\t9. (R) Live-set defect in a fetched register image refused before load.\n   371\t10. (H, R) `:unresolved-free` for a `:load-free` name the receiver cannot\n   372\t    resolve through primitives or modules.\n   373\t11. (H, R) `:shadowed-free` for a `:load-free` name shadowed by the\n   374\t    receiver's free environment or store.\n   375\t12. (R) Trusted fallback from R to H that names its trust in the outcome.\n   376\t13. (R) Verifying fallback that re-lowers named datoms, refuses a swapped\n   377\t    pairing with `:pairing-mismatch`, and accepts an authentic pairing.\n   378\t\n   379\tStructure:\n   380\t\n   381\t14. One fetch function serves both stack and register formats without\n   382\t    format-specific branching in `fetch`.\n   383\t15. Tests use an explicit `fetch` call; no `:call-hash` instruction is\n   384\t    emitted or consumed (deferred to B7).\n   385\t16. No global loader, registry, callback, or cache is introduced; handle\n   386\t    and index are explicit arguments.\n   387\t17. Tri-host parity: JVM, Node/CLJS, and ClojureDart pass all tests cleanly,\n   388\t    with 0 kondo errors and clean cljstyle formatting.\n1:# yin.vm de Bruijn linker over dao.stream (Phase B6)\n8:`dao.stream` (backed by `dao.jing` content addressing). It is Phase B6 of\n35:Phase B6 is implemented alone as the dedicated linker phase. It establishes\n149:;;               (not (jing/segment-matches? address value))\n165:   `(jing/segment-matches? address value)` verifies the value against the\n212: :free-names-fn yin.vm.debruijn-linker/stack-free-names}\n220:- `stack-free-names` is defined by the linker module (scanning `:load-free`\n230: :free-names-fn yin.vm.debruijn-linker/register-free-names}\n238:- `register-free-names` is defined by the linker module (scanning\n265:trust, and provenance. Phase B6 requires only a plain data value.\n319:## 10. File box: Phase B6\n324:    Depends on: dao.jing (segment-matches?, segment-key, materialize!, get),\n338:- `stack-free-names`: scans free names from stack instruction vectors.\n339:- `register-free-names`: scans free names from register image maps.\n343:## 11. Completion criteria: Phase B6\n362:   b. Corrupt client RPC response over DaoStream.\n364:   `make-get` filters invalid peer payloads, returning `:absent` if no peer\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
